.TH engraver\-config 1  "engraver 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
engraver\-config \- Manage configuration settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBengraver config\fR [\fB\-\-init\fR] [\fB\-\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
View and manage Engraver's persistent configuration settings.
When run without flags, displays the current configuration values.
.PP
Configuration settings provide default values for command-line options.
Command-line flags always take precedence over configuration file settings.
.PP
Each on/off setting has a flag that turns it on and a flag that turns it off,
so a setting that the file turns on can be turned off for one run:
.TP
\fBverify\fR in \fB[write]\fR
\fB\-\-verify\fR and \fB\-\-no\-verify\fR
.TP
\fBcheckpoint\fR in \fB[write]\fR
\fB\-\-checkpoint\fR and \fB\-\-no\-checkpoint\fR
.TP
\fBauto_detect\fR in \fB[checksum]\fR
\fB\-\-auto\-checksum\fR and \fB\-\-no\-auto\-checksum\fR
.TP
\fBskip_confirmation\fR in \fB[behavior]\fR
\fB\-y\fR or \fB\-\-yes\fR, and \fB\-\-confirm\fR
.TP
\fBquiet\fR in \fB[behavior]\fR
\fB\-q\fR or \fB\-\-quiet\fR, and \fB\-\-no\-quiet\fR
.TP
\fBjson\fR in \fB[benchmark]\fR
\fB\-\-json\fR and \fB\-\-no\-json\fR
.PP
If you give both flags of a pair, the last one wins.
\fB\-\-resume\fR with \fB\-\-no\-checkpoint\fR, and \fB\-\-silent\fR with
\fB\-\-confirm\fR, are usage errors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-init\fR
Create a new configuration file with default values.
Will not overwrite an existing configuration file.
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR
Print the path to the configuration file and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output current settings in JSON format for scripting.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The configuration file is located at:
.TP
\fBLinux:\fR
~/.config/engraver/engraver_config.toml, or
.br
\%$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/engraver/engraver_config.toml if \fB\%XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is set
.TP
\fBmacOS:\fR
~/Library/Application Support/engraver/engraver_config.toml
.TP
\fBWindows:\fR
%APPDATA%\\engraver\\engraver_config.toml
.PP
\fBengraver config \-\-path\fR prints the path Engraver uses.
A custom configuration file can be specified with the \fB\-\-config\-file\fR
global option.
.PP
Engraver finds the default file from \fBHOME\fR.
\fBsudo\fR usually sets \fBHOME\fR to root's home directory, so
\fBsudo engraver\fR reads root's configuration file, not yours.
To use your file under \fBsudo\fR, pass its path:
.PP
.nf
    sudo engraver \-\-config\-file "$(engraver config \-\-path)" write image.iso /dev/sdb
.fi
.SS Sections
.TP
\fB[write]\fR
Default block size, verify, checkpoint, retry settings, and read buffer size.
\fBread_buffer_size\fR applies to a local image file, plain or compressed.
\fBverify\fR compares a plain image in blocks of its \fB\-\-block\-size\fR instead.
\fBretry_attempts\fR and \fBretry_delay_ms\fR apply to \fBwrite\fR.
\fBerase\fR does not retry.
.TP
\fB[checksum]\fR
Default algorithm and auto-detection settings.
.TP
\fB[behavior]\fR
\fBskip_confirmation\fR answers yes to confirmation prompts, and \fBquiet\fR hides
progress and status output like \fB\-q\fR.
.TP
\fB[benchmark]\fR
Default block size, test size, data pattern, passes, and JSON output.
.TP
\fB[network]\fR
HTTP timeout, URL validation timeout, and cloud storage chunk size.
\fBhttp_timeout_secs\fR is how long to wait for an HTTP server to start answering,
and for each read of the body.
It does not cap the whole download.
.PP
A size must be a power of two, such as \fB"4M"\fR.
A timeout must be at least 1 second.
A size or timeout that can't be used stops \fBwrite\fR, \fBverify\fR, and
\fBchecksum\fR with an error that names the setting and the configuration file.
\fBlist\fR and \fBconfig\fR open no source and don't check these values.
.SH EXAMPLES
View current configuration:
.PP
.nf
    engraver config
.fi
.PP
Create a default configuration file:
.PP
.nf
    engraver config \-\-init
.fi
.PP
Show where the configuration file is stored:
.PP
.nf
    engraver config \-\-path
.fi
.PP
Pipe configuration as JSON to another tool:
.PP
.nf
    engraver config \-\-json | jq '.write.block_size'
.fi
.PP
Use a custom configuration file:
.PP
.nf
    engraver \-\-config\-file ./my\-config.toml write image.iso /dev/sdb
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBengraver\fR(1), \fBengraver\-write\fR(1), \fBengraver\-benchmark\fR(1)
